WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:09.690
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:19.890
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.450
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:06.920
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:14.190
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:20.970
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:28.330
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:05.520
<b>The Nearby War</b>

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:21.550
That wraps up
the patrol flight schedule.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:28.960
Have you authorized
mobilization of Chor Tempest?

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:34.100
We’re still flying?

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:38.650
You said we couldn’t gauge
Simoun chemistry otherwise, Morinas.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.020
I’ve had enough!
You’re amazing, Aer.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:44.350
So can we…

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:47.730
We haven’t done a Ri Majon yet.
Let’s try the Ray Ri Majon.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.530
Look at Aer go!

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.490
Morinas.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.000
It’s too complicated! I’m confused!

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:18.590
Morinas, focus.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.890
All right.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.470
Just wait… Wait.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:12.350
Chor Tempest is currently grounded
until its newest members arrive…

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.020
…Sibylla Aer.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.610
If we don’t practice,
it’ll be tough when trouble comes.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:23.200
Then use Similes.
After you’ve received permission.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.270
Aer! Morinas!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.170
Why’d you pray without permission?

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:38.670
It was a battle drill, not a prayer.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.420
Why are you scolding us?

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.190
You’re not even
the regina of Chor Tempest.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:52.580
The regina of our chor,
Neviril, is indisposed.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:54.920
In the meantime, I’m stepping in.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:59.920
Oh? Don’t tell me
that you and Sibylla Aurea…

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:02.940
…have that kind of special relationship.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:22.630
Aer! You forgot something!

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.980
The kiss of gratitude. After exiting
the Simoun, Tempus Spatium…

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:33.520
I couldn’t care less about that.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.340
Do you hate doing it with me?

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:46.030
Waporif, I’m sorry. We might’ve
gotten you in trouble too.

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:50.660
It’s our job to launch
Simouns when sibyllae request it.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.440
How cold.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.080
She’s a child. You needn’t tease her.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.380
Tease? Why would I?

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.180
But you know what? Flying with
that girl was simply wonderful.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.270
Aer.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:22.740
That was amazing, Aer.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.030
Which Ri Majon
were you trying before?

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:29.820
Aer, don’t do anything like that again.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.350
Why not? Are you all okay
with the way things are?

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:39.290
When will they put Chor Tempest
on duty to relieve the other chors?

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:42.040
At this rate…

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:46.300
If that happens, we can go back
to being normal Simoun sibyllae.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.930
Offering prayers and waiting
for our time to go to the Spring.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.470
The day I choose to become male.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:56.090
I can hardly wait, Big Sister.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:01.520
I’m planning to choose
the male gender myself, Alty.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.340
You all think so?

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:08.030
That it’s fine to not
go into battle anymore?

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:13.910
It’s Chor Rubor.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.370
Making a safe return
again today, I hope.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.810
You tried to do
the Ray Ri Majon, right?

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.720
You are a genius after all.

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:36.270
You can’t even do
a simple thing like that…

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:39.770
I wonder if this really
is Chor Tempest?

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:46.420
Is that how you feel too, Neviril?

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.400
That it doesn’t matter as long
as you don’t go into battle anymore?

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:54.130
How could anyone want to go to war?

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:57.260
Aer, we are merely…

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:02.100
…fulfilling our duties as priestesses
protecting Tempus Spatium.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:05.170
Then you fulfill that duty too!

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:11.130
Let me make myself clear.
Aer, you and I will never be a pair.

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.530
I’m Vura of Chor Rubor.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:29.830
We’ll be roommates starting today.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:34.030
Is that right? I’m Aer of Chor Tempest.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.910
You’re an auriga, right?

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:40.600
I am too.
Say, has that Neviril always been…

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:46.240
Since Chor Tempest is off active duty,
my chor’s been split into two units…

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.820
…doing patrol flights night and day.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.380
We don’t have the luxury
of lazing around like you people.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.420
Let me sleep.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:09.480
I bet I can fly in a way
that would satisfy even you.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:10.520
Perhaps.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:11.860
Then come with me.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.670
Everyone’s in
the cafeteria at this hour.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.710
But…

00:09:31.430 --> 00:09:34.720
It’s all right. I grabbed dinner for us.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.720
That’s not it…

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:39.590
What a pain in the butt…

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:42.470
Um…

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.600
Here, your half.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:45.680
Also…

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:49.690
Let’s go.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.690
Which Ri Majon first?

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:04.420
Which do you like?

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:06.360
I don’t know…

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:08.520
You must like one.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.750
The Silver Ri Majon… I guess.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:15.360
Yeah? That’s a good one.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.550
But if we’re going to,
let’s do it when we find the enemy.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:22.100
You’re going into battle?

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:27.260
If we do, they won’t be able
to ground our chor anymore.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:29.480
Isn’t that right?

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:31.700
You think so?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:33.980
Aer…

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.410
Is that…

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:55.090
It’s a Simoun.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:11:00.430
The new recruits in Chor Caput
are out on patrol tonight, right?

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.810
Why’s it there?

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.320
Maybe they were attacked.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:10.190
Then they’ve got info on the enemy.
Let’s make sure the area’s secure first.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:15.500
Just one unit.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.750
I’m in luck. This will be my last…

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:44.500
It has to be Aer!
And with Rimone this time!

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:47.720
Rimone? But that’s my pair…

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.010
She rejected me too.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.600
It’s not really
a matter of being rejected…

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.070
Another unauthorized flight?
I wish my chor had free time.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:02.710
This means the end of
Chor Tempest. We’re going to be busy.

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:04.910
Should we notify the dux?

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:08.080
If we don’t get them,
we’re all accountable.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.200
Why don’t we leave them alone?

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.420
If they want to fly,
we should let them fly.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:18.560
They’ll be back by morning.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:21.420
We can’t move
the Arcus Prima right now.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:26.180
Just what kind of
priestess is this Aer girl?

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.770
All that is certain…

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:33.830
…is that she has a reason.

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.810
A reason for being here.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:57.380
It’s a fake…

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:01.760
Rimone!

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:03.760
Aer!

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.430
Damn you…

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:16.190
That’s right.
We’re both Simoun sibyllae.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:21.190
So it’s true when they say that young
girls fly the Simouns in Kyuukoku.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:30.950
The disease is eating
away at our bodies.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:34.960
We are in need of new technology.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:38.130
The secret of Simouns,
hidden by Kyuukoku.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:40.180
If we can acquire that…

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:43.300
…we can bid farewell to
technology that pollutes the skies.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:05.280
I did it… I’ve taken a Simoun…

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:08.240
I’m not going to retire from the military!

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.160
Glory to Shoukoku!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:20.710
It’s useless!

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:26.260
You soldiers from Shoukoku aren’t
protected by Tempus Spatium!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:30.690
Only priestesses who haven’t gone
to the Spring can operate Simouns!

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:34.880
Only us, people who haven’t
decided on a gender yet!

00:14:37.190 --> 00:14:39.770
Tell me how to fly it!

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:42.770
Tell me!

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:24.770
Aer, what do we do?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:27.030
We retake the Simoun.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.690
Don’t talk so loud!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:34.250
He can’t understand our words anyway.
Shoukoku wants the Simouns.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:39.990
Since only Simouns fly freely through
the skies. But we can’t hand it over.

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.040
Aer…

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:47.360
All of my friends
have gone to the Spring.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.550
I’m the only one
in my village who hasn’t.

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.050
Why don’t you want to go, Aer?

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:59.650
Because I’m not sure. Whether I want
to become a man or stay a woman.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:03.410
If you go, they say Onasia
chooses if you haven’t decided.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:07.220
Having someone else choose
is worse! No, I don’t want that!

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:09.780
I can’t afford to make
mistakes in a place like this.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:13.280
I’ll become the best
Simoun sibylla of all.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:18.240
After all, as long as I fly a Simoun,
I won’t have to go to the Spring.

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.630
Tell me, young ladies…

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:29.960
How does it feel?
Not to be a man or woman?

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:33.380
You don’t understand, do you?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:40.060
I was turned male via medicine
and surgery right when I was born.

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:43.460
That’s the way things
are done in Shoukoku.

00:16:43.460 --> 00:16:46.690
That’s why I have no idea.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.030
Being born in a female body…

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:54.370
…and then being able to choose
whether to become a man or woman.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:56.610
How does that feel?

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.270
Do you think that man is ill?

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:57.890
Go! Fly!

00:17:57.890 --> 00:18:00.530
Come on, fly! What’s wrong, demon?

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:02.530
Why won’t you fly?

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:11.030
Sorry, young ladies.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.880
I can’t hand this over
to you. It’s mine now.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:20.250
If I can just take this back,
my country will usher in a new era.

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:22.840
The skies will clear…

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.620
No matter what, I’m going to…

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:39.570
Like I said, you can’t fly a Simoun.

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:44.000
His comrades might come for him.
In Shoukoku aircraft…

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:50.980
I won’t let him have it.
He’ll never take the Simoun.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.180
Help me get him down.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.810
We need to get back right away.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:36.150
He’s all stiff.

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:38.360
Let go! Let go! Let go, will you?

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.110
Don’t. It’ll break.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:50.210
I’m sure someone
will come looking for us…

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.810
Then we can…

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:52.670
No.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.810
We don’t know when the enemy will
come. We have to take off right away.

00:19:57.810 --> 00:20:02.180
And we can’t ever report that we
nearly got captured by the enemy.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:08.410
If only these hands on
the flight stick could be removed…

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.990
It can’t be helped…

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.520
It can’t be helped.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:18.020
Rimone, you can
go over there till I’m done.

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:22.030
Hurry! Go over there!

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:56.100
Ow…

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:04.750
Rimone!

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.950
Rimone! Help me carry him, Rimone!

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:10.670
Are you awake, Rimone?

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:12.410
Rimone!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.490
I guess I made trouble for you again.

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:56.040
As an apology,
we’ll clean it ourselves.

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:59.240
You don’t have to do that, Sibylla Aer.

00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:01.210
It’s fine. We want to.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:02.920
Rimone, if you please.

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:15.990
Taking on the task of
cleaning the Simoun themselves?

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:18.850
They’re starting to recognize
that they’re priestesses.

00:22:19.350 --> 00:22:20.440
You think so?

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:27.050
I’m sorry.

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:29.990
For getting you so dirty.

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:47.820
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:52.060
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.060 --> 00:22:59.130
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.130 --> 00:23:06.930
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:19.610
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:24.790
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.790 --> 00:23:28.800
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:32.770
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:38.060
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:44.220
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:47.680
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:53.320
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:59.480
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:12.510
Will Dominüra be up
to the task of guiding Rimone?

00:24:14.670 --> 00:24:16.430
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>White Loneliness</b>

00:24:16.430 --> 00:24:17.930
White Loneliness.
